{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T09:01:55.397Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `osq sync <id>` and its core:\n\n- **`src/core/vcs/sync-change.ts`** (new): `syncChange` implements \"Sync on request\" — refuses vcs-off/NoVcs, unknown change, running task, awaited stacked dependency, and a dirty worktree, in the spec's order; otherwise runs `syncWithDefaultBranch` and returns the merged/already-current line. A stop of an active change records an uncommitted `sync_stopped` event; archived changes record nothing.\n- **`src/cli/sync.ts`** (new): `syncCommand` / `registerSyncCommand`, shaped like `land.ts` with injectable `cwd`, `config`, `stdout`, `stderr`, `exit`, loading config inside error handling.\n- **`src/cli/index.ts`**: registers `sync` next to `registerLandCommand`.\n- **`README.md`**: one paragraph after `osq message` and before the walkthrough.\n- **`tests/vcs-sync-command.test.ts`** (new): 12 tests over real temp repos covering every \"Sync on request\" and \"Sync command\" scenario plus the extra refusals.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --test tests/vcs-sync-command.test.ts` → 12/12 pass.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` → `EXIT=0` (2702 CLI tests + 94 UI tests, 0 fail; typechecks, build, lint clean).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/110-osq-sync/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nOne noted gap: the task referenced an `appendSyncEvent` helper in `sync-main.ts` that does not exist; I wrote a local `appendSyncStopped` in `sync-change.ts` matching the existing event shape (recorded under `## Missing context`)."}}
